# The built binary, at the repository root only. Written without a leading
# slash, this matched any path COMPONENT named openflux - including the iOS
# app's own source directory ios-app/OpenFlux/, which silently dropped twelve
# files from the tree. Because core.ignorecase is true on Windows and false on
# Linux, the same repository contained the iOS sources on one platform and not
# on the other, so a clone built on each produced a different project.
# Verified with git check-ignore -v: the rule matched
# ios-app/OpenFlux/... and nothing at the root.
/openflux
*.bak
